#: <RELIC_ROOT>/docs/source/public/science/pedosphere.md
msgid "Water-filled pore space WFPS_thr above which the denitrification anaerobic factor rises, f_anoxic = max(clip((WFPS - WFPS_thr)/w, 0, 1), f_min) with w = pedosphere.denitrification.anaerobic_transition_width and f_min = pedosphere.denitrification.minimum_anaerobic_factor. Linn and Doran (1984) found aerobic microbial activity maximal at 60 percent WFPS and declining above it through reduced aeration; DAYCENT (Del Grosso et al. 2000) drives denitrification with WFPS. Bounds: nitrification is the main N2O source up to 60 percent and denitrification produced all N2O at 70 percent WFPS (Bateman and Baggs 2005); 0.8 keeps the ramp inside the unit interval."
msgstr "反硝化厌氧因子开始上升的水填充孔隙比例 WFPS_thr，f_anoxic = max(clip((WFPS - WFPS_thr)/w, 0, 1), f_min)，其中 w = pedosphere.denitrification.anaerobic_transition_width，f_min = pedosphere.denitrification.minimum_anaerobic_factor。Linn and Doran (1984) 发现好氧微生物活性在 60% WFPS 时最大，超过该值后因通气减弱而下降；DAYCENT（Del Grosso et al. 2000）采用 WFPS 驱动反硝化。边界依据：WFPS 不超过 60% 时硝化是主要 N2O 来源，70% WFPS 时全部 N2O 均来自反硝化（Bateman and Baggs 2005）；0.8 保证线性上升段处于单位区间内。"

#: <RELIC_ROOT>/docs/source/public/science/pedosphere.md
msgid "Source: literature; Linn, D.M. and Doran, J.W. (1984) Effect of water-filled pore space on carbon dioxide and nitrous oxide production in tilled and nontilled soils, Soil Sci. Soc. Am. J. 48, 1267-1272, doi:10.2136/sssaj1984.03615995004800060013x; Del Grosso, S.J., Parton, W.J., Mosier, A.R., Ojima, D.S., Kulmala, A.E. and Phongpan, S. (2000) General model for N2O and N2 gas emissions from soils due to dentrification, Global Biogeochem. Cycles 14, 1045-1060, doi:10.1029/1999GB001225"
msgstr "来源：文献； Linn, D.M. and Doran, J.W. (1984) Effect of water-filled pore space on carbon dioxide and nitrous oxide production in tilled and nontilled soils, Soil Sci. Soc. Am. J. 48, 1267-1272, doi:10.2136/sssaj1984.03615995004800060013x; Del Grosso, S.J., Parton, W.J., Mosier, A.R., Ojima, D.S., Kulmala, A.E. and Phongpan, S. (2000) General model for N2O and N2 gas emissions from soils due to dentrification, Global Biogeochem. Cycles 14, 1045-1060, doi:10.1029/1999GB001225"

